# Flutter conventions

`apps/mobile` is the iOS and Android participant app. `apps/admin` is the Flutter web admin app. Keep them separate. Shared HTTP types and the JWT client live in `packages/api_client`.

- Route with `go_router`.
- Read `APP_ENV`, `API_BASE_URL`, `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`, and `APPLE_CLIENT_ID` from `--dart-define` via `AppConfig`. Hide Google/Apple buttons when those client IDs are empty.
- Keep English (`en`) and Simplified Chinese (`zh_Hans` ARB / `zh-Hans` API) files in `lib/l10n`. Send `zh-Hans` to the API. Do not use `zh` alone for API locale.
- Generate localizations from `l10n.yaml`. Do not hardcode user-facing strings in widgets.
- Keep business rules on the backend. Flutter validates format only (identifier shape, password length, required fields).
- Use the inherited `SessionController` / `ApiScope` already in the apps. Do not add a new state-management framework.

```sh
flutter run --dart-define=APP_ENV=development --dart-define=API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000/api/v1
```
